# A method executes its own named Structure (OPUS-Q54-CONTINUE-20260929-14 slice 2c; book §9 after 55c1abc: `S` and
# `S()` call S; §12: a named Structure is a procedure without arguments).  S's procedure is a method of its own -- its
# own fields S's fields, in S's slots -- registered with the method's entries, after the entry E, so it has no unit
# child: its occurrence is S itself, built at S's statement with the procedure's trampoline as its native word
# (pinned).  The call is lmx_call_prim(S, S) (pinned): owner = data = S, so `node` in S's body is S's parent, the
# method's occurrence.  S's body here is its field declaration, and every call -- `S()`, `S: ()`, the bare `S` -- stores
# its initializer again: S\v, written 9 before each, reads 4 after each.  Was unit_local_ns_call_refused.  Entry 7.
fn: m () int
    S:
        size_t: v 4U
    S\v: 9U
    S()
    size_t: a 9U
    a: S\v
    S\v: 9U
    S: ()
    size_t: b 9U
    b: S\v
    S\v: 9U
    S
    size_t: c 9U
    c: S\v
    int: r 0
    if: a = 4U && b = 4U && c = 4U
        r: 7
    int: out r
    return: out
end: m
int: r 0
r: m()
sendMessage: exit(exit_code: r; stdout: ""; stderr: "")
return
